<https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-interaction-record/26> a prov:Entity, ms:PublicInteractionRecord, ms:PublicProjectionNode;
    ms:turn 26;
    ms:worldId "world_001_nocturne".
<https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-record/26/grounded/1> a prov:Entity, ms:GroundedPublicFact, ms:PublicProjectionNode;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-interaction-record/26>;
    ms:surface "Held to the lamp, every leaf of the nocturne shows the same heron watermark — the Brell mill's mark.".
<https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-record/26/grounded/2> a prov:Entity, ms:GroundedPublicFact, ms:PublicProjectionNode;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-interaction-record/26>;
    ms:surface "The steward's stock-book is plain: heron paper entered the copy-room in the winter of the flood, and the last of it was spent before the thaw. None before, none since.".
<https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-record/26/grounded/3> a prov:Entity, ms:GroundedPublicFact, ms:PublicProjectionNode;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-interaction-record/26>;
    ms:surface "The night porter remembers the flood winter well: the copy-room lamps burned past midnight, week upon week, and it was the archive girl, Liane, who kept them burning.".
<https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-record/26/grounded/4> a prov:Entity, ms:GroundedPublicFact, ms:PublicProjectionNode;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-interaction-record/26>;
    ms:surface "Played through once, the nocturne gives up its middle voice: it carries an older tune entire — a cradle-song, set like a keepsake under the right hand's figures.".
<https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-record/26/grounded/5> a prov:Entity, ms:GroundedPublicFact, ms:PublicProjectionNode;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-interaction-record/26>;
    ms:surface "Mistress Odile knows the tune at one hearing: the Vara cradle-song, never printed, never performed, sung only within that house's walls.".
<https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-record/26/grounded/6> a prov:Entity, ms:GroundedPublicFact, ms:PublicProjectionNode;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-interaction-record/26>;
    ms:surface "Liane was raised within the Vara house — the music-master's orphan, taken in as ward; she grew up under that roof and under its songs.".
<https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-record/26/hypotheses/1> a prov:Entity, ms:LearnerHypothesis, ms:PublicProjectionNode;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://machinespirits.org/derivation/world/world_001_nocturne/public-interaction-record/26>;
    ms:text "Liane had both opportunity and access, but the correcting hand is still missing.";
    ms:turn 23.
